'''Candy Paradise''' (カルメ桃源郷 ''Karume Tōgenkyō'', '''Karume Utopia''') is the 12th sub-chapter of [[Zero Legends]], and the 110th sub-chapter overall. It was introduced in [[Version 13.4 Update|Version 13.4]] and is available up to {{2c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
One of the most straightforward Zero Legends sub-chapters yet. The odd-numbered stages are [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]-heavy stages that can easily be thwarted by standard [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie Cats]] like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]. The even-numbered stages focus on [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sages]] and require slightly more effort, with the hardest overall arguably being [[Pointed Lakeshore]], a fight against [[Dark Dober]] and [[Oldhorn]] with [[Gory Dark]]s, [[Trolly Blogger]]s and [[Dogenstein]]s as peons.
{{LegendDiff|120}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces 2 enemies to Zero Legends:
*[[Doctor K.O.]]: A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Kang Roo]]. Similar to a 300% [[Shadow Boxer K]], but with only 3 knockbacks, higher health (20k less than a [[Bore]]), range and speed.
*[[CTO Seal]]: A Red variant of [[Otta-smack-u]] from [[Worker's Revolution (Monthly Event)|Worker's Revolution]]. Fairly durable and attacks non-stop from 380 range, constantly applying a 4-second freeze to all units hit.

